  "notes": [
    "Original late/early run completed both modes before preload was rejected by an overly strict label-location audit. The pre-launch audit was corrected to recognize indented scoped PTX labels, and preload was run separately. No generated kernel arithmetic changed.",
    "The preload variant adds a first-weight-tile load and loop reuse before waiting. It increases registers and changes the compiler software pipeline; this negative result applies to these tested implementations, not every possible PDL design.",
    "Every PDL destination uses griddepcontrol.wait before dependent loads. Pre-wait loads in preload are traced to the independent W pointer or W tensor descriptor in emitted PTX; compile hooks audit before initial launch. Graph edges are created by launch_pdl, not manually rewritten.",
    "Retained baseline graph cache identities do not change during patched candidate contexts, and baseline graph audits contain zero PDL kernels or programmatic edges."
  ]
